      "documentConcept": "Deep brain stimulation (STN/GPi): patient selection and programming",
      "canonicalConceptId": "concept:e7f58f92a50cfeb448150d6cf5992437be0309496411aa49022604159f452999",
      "text": "STN and GPi DBS selection depends on the patient\u2019s disabling symptoms, levodopa response, neuropsychological risks and treatment goals. Both targets can improve motor symptoms; medication-reduction goals favor STN, while selected dyskinesia and cognitive or mood concerns can favor GPi. Interdisciplinary evaluation and realistic expectations are central. Programming uses contact testing and adjustment of amplitude, pulse width and frequency, supported by device checks and coordinated medication management. Comparative cognitive findings depend on the study and stimulation setting, and axial symptoms require separate counseling.",
